\import{base-macros}

\p{What M8 delivers, where it deviates from [design-isa-document](design-isa-document) / \code{\verb~|WORK-PACKAGES.md~} and why, what was measured, and what is not done. The tools are in the test tree (\code{\verb~|Quote~}, \code{\verb~|TierEq~}, \code{\verb~|Diff~}, \code{\verb~|M8*~}), the scripts in \code{\verb~|src/test/resources/m8/~}, the reports in \code{\verb~|work/status/~}.}

\subtree{
\title{1. Commands (one per report)}

\p{\code{\verb~|rlvm-machine/src/test/resources/m8/report.sh --help~} lists them. Every command measures the \strong{main tree as published}: the script copies the module in a moment without a publication (checked against \code{\verb~|work/sandbox/.lock.holder~} and \code{\verb~|publish.log~} before and after the copy; it does not queue behind the publications), compiles the copy and runs \code{\verb~|rlvm.machine.M8Main~} in a JVM of its own (\code{\verb~|-Xss2m~}, 6g heap, \code{\verb~|-Xmn1g~}, inside one host-wide slot of \src{bench/slot.sh}, pinned to the CPUs outside the measurement container; wave 6, section 7). It never runs Maven on the main tree and never writes into it. \code{\verb~|--tree work/sandbox/Mk/rlvm-machine~} measures a sandbox instead (your files before you publish them).}

\p{\strong{Wave 6 added the three commands everybody uses now (section 7): \code{\verb~|report.sh gate~}, \code{\verb~|report.sh mutants~}, \code{\verb~|ladder.py measure~}, and \code{\verb~|big.py~} for the large corpora.}}

\table{
\tr{\th{Command}\th{Report in \code{\verb~|work/status/~}}\th{What (ISA section 11; stepper-convention H12)}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|report.sh tutorial~} / \code{\verb~|bugs~} / \code{\verb~|all~} / \code{\verb~|init~} (\code{\verb~|gates~} = these four)}\td{\code{\verb~|machine-diff-NAME.txt~}}\td{machine against the reference engine, per declaration, in-process: the v0 gate. First lines: \code{\verb~|GATE NAME: DIFF-CLEAN / NOT CLEAN / WRONG VERDICTS~}, counts, what stopped the machine how often (stub, error code), then one line per file and the first difference of every file with its reproduction command. Exit 1 = a wrong verdict}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|report.sh std~} / \code{\verb~|cedar~} / \code{\verb~|reachability~}, \code{\verb~|report.sh diff NAME PATH..~}}\td{the same}\td{v1 gate, the Cedar-level slices, any corpus}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|report.sh launcher tutorial~} / \code{\verb~|bugs~} / \code{\verb~|all~}}\td{\code{\verb~|machine-launcher-NAME.txt~}}\td{the gate in its own form: every test through \code{\verb~|work/dist/bin/rlvm-jvm --threads 1 -X engine=machine~} with the published jar on \code{\verb~|RLVM_EXTRA_CP~}; the verdict against the arena's classification AND \code{\verb~|values.engine.primary.machine.declined == 0~}, \code{\verb~|units.declined == 0~} from the statistics (the exit status alone proves nothing)}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|report.sh conv NAME~}}\td{\code{\verb~|machine-conv-NAME.txt~}}\td{convention equivalence (H12 item 1): every declaration under host depth bounds \code{\verb~|Op.HOST_DEPTH~} (128), 64, 0 and unbounded: outcome, reason, ticks, call events by op, the frame trace; after an ACCEPT every record word (ids, flags, memo words), every run word, the pair entries}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|report.sh frames NAME~}}\td{\code{\verb~|machine-frames-NAME.txt~}, \code{\verb~|machine-calls-NAME.tsv~}}\td{call events and frames written per declaration under the bound in force; the bound of H12 item 2 (frames below 0.1\% of the calls, on Init); the per-declaration call table is compared with the previous one (+2\% alert of ISA section 11)}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|report.sh sample NAME~}}\td{\code{\verb~|machine-sample-NAME.txt~}}\td{judgment level: \code{\verb~|infer~}, \code{\verb~|whnf~}, \code{\verb~|whnfCore~}, \code{\verb~|isDefEq~}, \code{\verb~|isProp~}, \code{\verb~|ensurePi~} of the machine on sampled sub-terms (binders opened on the way), read back with \code{\verb~|Quote~} and judged by the reference kernel up to its \code{\verb~|isDefEq~}}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|report.sh tiers NAME~}}\td{\code{\verb~|machine-tiers-NAME.txt~}}\td{K0 against the tier \code{\verb~|-Dm8.k1=facts,tele,code,casetrees~}: DELTA, WHNF, VTYPE give the same value and CONV the same answer on generated applications of every constant}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|report.sh cost --stage LABEL [--runs N] [CORPUS..]~}}\td{\code{\verb~|machine-cost.md~}, \code{\verb~|machine-cost.tsv~}}\td{the per-stage table CPU / wall / RSS / instructions (in that order): machine and reference engine through the launcher in the arena-shaped container (\src{bench/measure.sh}), ratio to the reference and to gruszka. A machine row whose engine checks fell back to the reference kernel is marked FALLBACK}}
\tr{\td{\code{\verb~|convcost.sh micro~}, \code{\verb~|convcost.sh corpus CORPUS..~}}\td{\code{\verb~|machine-convcost-micro.txt~}, rows \code{\verb~|convcost~} in \code{\verb~|machine-cost.md~}}\td{CPU cost of \code{\verb~|m.hostDepth~} as a field and of the masked TICK line (section 4)}}
}

\p{In a sandbox the same code runs as tests (\code{\verb~|scripts/machine-sandbox.sh test Mk ...~}):}

\pre{\verb~|
-Dgroups=slow -DexcludedGroups= -Dtest='M8DiffReportTest#tutorial'        (#bugs #all #init #std #cedar #custom)
-Dgroups=slow -DexcludedGroups= -Dtest='M8SlowTest#convTutorial'          (#convBugs #framesInit #sampleInit #tiersValuesTutorial ..)
-Dtest=M8DiffOneTest -Dm8.file=FILE [-Dm8.unit=N] [-Dm8.all=true] [-Dm8.trace=true]   one file in detail: both outcomes,
                                                                          reasons, ticks, call events by op, frames, trace
-Dtest='M8ConventionTest#oneFile' -Dm8.file=FILE                          convention equivalence of one file
-Dtest='M8SamplerTest#oneFile' -Dm8.file=FILE [-Dm8.unit=U] [-Dm8.seed=S] one sampled difference again
~}

\p{Options everywhere (system properties): \code{\verb~|-Dm8.hostDepth=0~}, \code{\verb~|-Dm8.switches=warm,gated~}, \code{\verb~|-Dm8.debug=..~}, \code{\verb~|-Dm8.maxSteps=N~}, \code{\verb~|-Dm8.checkSeconds=N~}, \code{\verb~|-Dm8.fileSeconds=N~}, \code{\verb~|-Dm8.suffix=-d0~} (report name), \code{\verb~|-Dm8.seed=N~}, \code{\verb~|-Dm8.perConstant=N~}, \code{\verb~|-Dm8.every=N~}, \code{\verb~|-Dm8.k1=..~}.}

\p{Guard of every publication (fast group): \code{\verb~|M8GateTest~} = no SOUNDNESS / COMPLETENESS difference on a fixed sample of tutorial and \code{\verb~|bugs/~} files (declines pass). It fails the publication of whoever introduces a wrong verdict and prints the reproduction command.}
}

\subtree{
\title{2. What the pieces are}

\ul{
\li{\code{\verb~|M8Harness~}: one loaded export, the reference engine, and any number of machine configurations ("lanes": host depth, switches, debug modes) run over its units in lockstep. Every lane has its own worker context over the same store; an observing \code{\verb~|Session~} sits between admission and \code{\verb~|MachineSession.check~} and records outcome, ticks, call events by op, frames, the trace, and after an ACCEPT digests of records, runs and pairs; every check has a deadline that the machine sees through its 4096-tick poll.}
\li{\code{\verb~|Diff~}: the corpus runner and the report.}
\li{\code{\verb~|TierEq~}: \code{\verb~|conventionEquivalence(path)~}, \code{\verb~|compare(machineA, machineB)~} (word-for-word comparison of two machines, with the first difference printed), \code{\verb~|traceDifference~}, the reports \code{\verb~|conv~} and \code{\verb~|frames~}, \code{\verb~|tierEquivalence(path, seed)~} (declaration outcomes under two switch sets).}
\li{\code{\verb~|Quote~}: readback of a value into the overlay. Closures and suspensions by substitution of the frame and of \code{\verb~|ls~} (no judgment runs); a PII through \code{\verb~|DOM~} / \code{\verb~|OPEN~} / \code{\verb~|INST~}; in-scope FVARs as the loose variables of their binders, or as a term given with \code{\verb~|Quote.of(m).local(fvar, term)~}; a HOLE slot that the term turns out to read is reported (mask contract, ISA 2.4).}
\li{\code{\verb~|M8Sampler~}: glue between \code{\verb~|rlvm.testkit.KernelSampler~}, M6's \code{\verb~|MachineOps~} (with \code{\verb~|Quote::quote~} as its quoter) and a \code{\verb~|RefKernel~} on the same worker context.}
\li{\code{\verb~|M8Tiers~}: tier equivalence on values, by a structural fingerprint that includes closure identity.}
\li{\code{\verb~|M8ConvCost~}: the micro-benchmark of section 4.}
}
}

\subtree{
\title{3. Deviations}

\table{
\tr{\th{\verb~|#~}\th{Where}\th{Deviation}\th{Reason}}
\tr{\td{D1}\td{\code{\verb~|Diff.run~}, the reports}\td{the corpus runs go through \code{\verb~|M8Harness~} (own loader wiring, one worker context per lane, an observing \code{\verb~|Session~}), not through \code{\verb~|Fixture.diffAgainstReference()~} as WORK-PACKAGES M8 says}\td{a report over hundreds of files needs per-declaration observation, a deadline per check, a hard limit per file and several machines over one store; the fixture is a frozen shared file. The counting rule is the fixture's (\code{\verb~|M8HarnessTest.theHarnessCountsAsTheFixtureDoes~}), except D8. \code{\verb~|Diff.file(path)~} still is the fixture's comparison}}
\tr{\td{D2}\td{\code{\verb~|Diff.directory~}}\td{returns the rendered report; \code{\verb~|Diff.run~} / \code{\verb~|Diff.report~} return the structured one}\td{the stub's \code{\verb~|String~} signature is kept}}
\tr{\td{D3}\td{convention equivalence}\td{after an outcome other than ACCEPT only outcome, reason, ticks, call events and the trace are compared, not records and memo words}\td{\code{\verb~|MachineSession.check~} resets the machine before it returns such an outcome (ISA 14.1); the comparison goes through the real facade on purpose}}
\tr{\td{D4}\td{convention equivalence}\td{the pair table is compared as a set of \code{\verb~|(lo, hi, status)~}; another insertion order is counted as a note}\td{ISA 1.3 names "memo and pair-table contents", not the order of the insertion log}}
\tr{\td{D5}\td{lane without a depth bound}\td{a \code{\verb~|StackOverflowError~} in the unbounded lane makes that declaration "not compared" (counted); under a bound it is not caught}\td{plain host recursion is a test configuration (H9); under a bound an overflow is a defect and must stay loud (ISA 12 R11)}}
\tr{\td{D6}\td{the reports' JVM}\td{\code{\verb~|-Xss2m~} like surefire's; the conv run uses one 64 MiB thread for its three lanes}\td{the machine must not need a deep host stack (H9); only the unbounded lane does}}
\tr{\td{D7}\td{deadlines}\td{a machine check that runs longer than \code{\verb~|m8.checkSeconds~} (default 120) is cancelled through \code{\verb~|RunSignals.firstFailure()~} at the next 4096-tick poll and counts as a decline (CANCELLED); a file beyond \code{\verb~|m8.fileSeconds~} (default 1800) is reported as TIMEOUT}\td{a report must survive a looping judgment. A loop that never ticks is only caught by the file limit (the line says so). On a loaded host a slow, correct check can be cancelled: read the reason column before reading a decline as a defect}}
\tr{\td{D8}\td{a unit the reference engine DECLINES}\td{not SOUNDNESS / COMPLETENESS whatever the machine says; counted as "reference declined"; the run goes on behind it; the file is settled by the official verdict (the arena's good / bad classification, confirmed by the official checker for all 230 tests): \code{\verb~|CLEAN*~} if the machine's verdict of the file is the official one, \code{\verb~|WRONG~} if it is the opposite. The reference engine gets the driver's budget (min(6 GiB, 60\% of the heap))}\td{M5's request of 08:57Z: \code{\verb~|perf/app-lam~} and \code{\verb~|perf/magma-list-deep-n36~} exhaust a 4 GiB budget of the reference engine; without this the \code{\verb~|all~} gate could never be clean and a real soundness line would hide among such lines. The shared fixture follows since 09:31Z (\code{\verb~|DiffReport.referenceDeclined~}, M6); one difference remains: the fixture's \code{\verb~|clean()~} is false for a file with such a unit, the harness settles it by the official verdict}}
\tr{\td{D9}\td{\code{\verb~|Quote~}}\td{closures and suspensions are read back by substitution (\code{\verb~|TermOps.instantiate~} of the frame's readbacks, then \code{\verb~|instantiateLevelParams~} by \code{\verb~|ls~}), not by evaluating the body under a fresh variable; the memo is keyed by (value, number of open binders) for OPEN values and dropped when the machine was reset, the overlay shrank, the open binders changed or a local changed}\td{the term is what the value \em{means} (ISA 2.2), independent of how well the machine evaluates: the right thing to hand to the reference kernel, and no judgment runs (a readback must not perturb what it observes more than necessary). Only a PII has no term of its own and is read back through \code{\verb~|INST~}}}
\tr{\td{D10}\td{\code{\verb~|Quote~}}\td{a NatStore literal is read back as \code{\verb~|b.termOf(Nat.transfer(m.nats, handle, b.store()))~}}\td{M6's request of 08:48Z (the machine's number overlay)}}
\tr{\td{D11}\td{sampler}\td{the comparison is \code{\verb~|rlvm.testkit.KernelSampler~} (not a second walker in this module); it needs \code{\verb~|MachineOps~} (M6). A judgment that ends in a stub is counted by stub, not as a difference; the report then says NO DATA, not AGREE. \code{\verb~|Tally.more~} (isProp / whnfCore / ensurePi) is read reflectively: the published test-kit jar is older than its source}\td{one sampler for the launcher campaign (\code{\verb~|testkit diff --sample~}) and for this module}}
\tr{\td{D12}\td{tier equivalence}\td{"the same value id" across K0 and K1 is tested as "the same structural fingerprint" (kind, components, and for closures the term id, \code{\verb~|ls~} and the fingerprints of the frame slots incl. HOLE and the REST run) in two sessions of one machine; results equal up to PEEK are counted, not failed}\td{a memo written by one tier must not answer the other, so the tiers cannot share a session; with canonical ids a common fingerprint is a common id (I-ID). The up-to-PEEK relaxation follows M2's note of 08:56Z}}
\tr{\td{D14}\td{report names}\td{the plain names (\code{\verb~|machine-diff-tutorial.txt~}, ..) are written only by runs on the main tree; a run on a sandbox (\code{\verb~|report.sh --tree ..~}, or a slow M8 test inside a sandbox) gets the suffix \code{\verb~|-Mk~} unless \code{\verb~|-Dm8.suffix~} is given and says "MEASURED: THE SANDBOX .., NOT THE MAIN TREE" in its header}\td{other packages ran the reports on their sandboxes (as intended) and overwrote the gate reports the orchestrator reads}}
\tr{\td{D15}\td{convention lanes}\td{\code{\verb~|TierEq.BOUNDS~} = \code{\verb~|Op.HOST_DEPTH~} (128 since 10:29Z, M6's decision on the frame counts of section 5), 64, 0, unbounded; the first is the lane the others are compared with}\td{H12 item 1 and the acceptance of M8 name D = 64 and D = 0; the bound in force moved}}
\tr{\td{D13}\td{\code{\verb~|M8GateTest~}}\td{a fast test of M8 asserts something about all packages together: no wrong verdict on 25 files}\td{WORK-PACKAGES section 6: soundness + completeness must be 0 at every commit. It never asserts that a stub throws}}
}
}

\subtree{
\title{4. Measured}

\p{Host: aarch64, 20 cores, shared with the other 15 agents of the wave (load average 100-150 while these were taken); figures are minima over rounds where stated.}

\p{\strong{Cost of the skeleton's two deviations from the measured convention} (NOTES-M6 S3, S4), requested by the skeleton. \code{\verb~|convcost.sh micro~} (\code{\verb~|work/status/machine-convcost-micro.txt~}): toy judgments that differ only in the depth test and the TICK line, CPU time per judgment, minimum of 25 interleaved rounds.}

\table{
\tr{\th{JIT}\th{workload}\th{CP: constant bound, \code{\verb~|--m.fuel < 0~} (the convention)}\th{FP: field bound}\th{CM: masked TICK}\th{FM: as built}\th{as built / convention}}
\tr{\td{C2 (the launcher today)}\td{a judgment that only makes two sub-calls}\td{1.42 ns}\td{1.45 ns}\td{1.74 ns}\td{1.76 ns}\td{1.24}}
\tr{\td{C2}\td{the same with one intern probe per judgment}\td{5.37 ns}\td{5.36 ns}\td{5.69 ns}\td{5.70 ns}\td{1.06}}
\tr{\td{Graal JIT}\td{two sub-calls}\td{1.74 ns}\td{1.81 ns}\td{1.73 ns}\td{1.74 ns}\td{1.00}}
\tr{\td{Graal JIT}\td{with one intern probe}\td{6.09 ns}\td{6.10 ns}\td{6.21 ns}\td{6.23 ns}\td{1.02}}
}

\p{Reading: \code{\verb~|m.hostDepth~} as a field is free (at most 0.03 ns, inside the noise). The masked TICK line costs about 0.3 ns per ticking judgment under C2 and about 0.1 ns under the Graal JIT: a quarter of a judgment that does nothing, 6\% of one that interns one record.}

\p{\strong{The same on the real machine} (\code{\verb~|convcost.sh corpus --runs 6 init~}, rows \code{\verb~|convcost~} of \code{\verb~|work/status/machine-cost.md~}): three variant jars built by \code{\verb~|sed~} from the main tree of 10:04Z (35 depth tests, 41 TICK lines replaced), Init through the launcher (C2, one worker, arena-shaped container), minimum CPU time of six runs each; all four accept all 57,938 declarations:}

\table{
\tr{\th{variant}\th{CPU s (6 runs)}\th{CPU s (first series, 2 runs)}\th{instructions G}}
\tr{\td{as built (field bound, masked TICK)}\td{15.01}\td{15.36}\td{151.1}}
\tr{\td{constant bound}\td{15.51}\td{16.31}\td{157.3}}
\tr{\td{plain TICK (\code{\verb~|--m.fuel < 0~}, no poll)}\td{15.19}\td{15.92}\td{154.8}}
\tr{\td{constant bound and plain TICK (the convention)}\td{14.88}\td{14.63}\td{153.5}}
}

\p{No consistent order: the variant with only the constant bound is slower than the machine as built, the one with both changes is 0.9\% faster. The resolution of this host (load average 130-180 during the runs) is about 3\%, and the differences are inside it. The micro-benchmark bounds the effect from above: 0.33 ns x 94 M ticks = 31 ms of 15 s = 0.2\%. \strong{Conclusion: neither deviation has a measurable CPU cost on Init.} If it ever matters, the plain line can keep the poll: let \code{\verb~|fuel~} count down a chunk of at most 4096 ticks and let \code{\verb~|tickSlow()~} refill it from a reserve after polling (\code{\verb~|ticks() = tickBase - fuel - reserve~}); the TICK line is then the convention's \code{\verb~|--m.fuel < 0~}. Not requested: the measured cost does not justify touching every judgment.}
}

