\p{The declines: 386 + 5 declarations that enter eager reduction (UNSUPPORTED_INPUT; Init 164, Std 203, reachability 8, Cedar slice 11, perf/grind-ring-5 4, bugs/rec-of-subst-prop 1), perf/loop-unfolded-once (E_MEM at 2^28 run words, as in wave 5) and perf/magma-list-deep-n36 \code{\verb~|countermodel~} (the report's 6 GiB heap: \code{\verb~|Machine.heapAllows~} refused a 1 GiB array; \code{\verb~|--heap 12g~} checks it). Frames written under D128: Init 0.051\%, Std 0.047\%, Cedar slice 0.026\%, reachability 1.14\%.}

\p{Found by the gate on the way (quick form, tutorial + bugs + Cedar slice, \code{\verb~|warm,gated,expect~}, tree of 14:46Z): bad/bugs/rec-of-subst-prop unit 128 \code{\verb~|Issue.forallFalse~}: lane \code{\verb~|memocheck,shortcheck~} E_AUDIT ("CONV .. is memoised as HOLE/T but the re-computation gives NONE/F") and the generic tier rejecting for another reason than the warm tier: the warm-session / eager-reduction defect that M5 and M6 reported in the same quarter of an hour (F26); it led to the rule "a declaration that enters eager reduction is declined".}

\p{Full gate of \code{\verb~|warm,gated,expect~} (4 MiB session cap), the same tree (\code{\verb~|work/m8/machine-gate-step1-1609Z.md~}; 65 minutes wall): \strong{PASS WITH DECLINES}, the declines being exactly those of the generic tier. Differential: SOUNDNESS 0, COMPLETENESS 0 on every corpus (all 230: 15,798 accepted, 40 rejected, 7 declined; Init 57,774 / 164 declined; Std 99,893 / 203; reachability 4,216 / 8; Cedar slice 8,053 / 11). Tier equivalence against the generic tier: 0 declarations with another outcome, 0 with another reason. Convention equivalence with warm sessions: 0 differences (12 perf declarations not compared with the unbounded lane); frames under D128: Init 0.072\%, Std 0.064\%, Cedar slice 0.41\%, reachability 1.15\%. Audits: 0 outcome differences, 0 \code{\verb~|E_AUDIT~}. Pipeline: 230 / 230 verdicts right, the four corpora accepted with 4 workers, MACHINE-INCOMPLETE 0, WARM-ANOMALY 0, disagreements 0.}

\p{\strong{Finding M8-F1 (17:35Z-17:55Z, open; requests.log to M2 and M7).} The quick gate of \code{\verb~|warm,gated,expect,probes,code,casetrees~} on the tree of about 17:30Z FAILS on convention equivalence and on nothing else (differential 0 / 0, generic tier equal, tier test on values 175 constants / 700 results equal, audits clean, pipeline right): on the Cedar slice two of 8,064 declarations (unit 6225 \code{\verb~|Cedar.Thm.conversion_preserves_typedness._unary~}, unit 7434 \code{\verb~|Cedar.Thm.ofEnv_entities_valid_refs_for_wt_expr._unary~}) use one tick more under host depth 0 than under D128 (two with \code{\verb~|probes~}); the lane without a bound agrees with D128. Bisected with \code{\verb~|report.sh gate --switches S --parts conv cedar~}: clean for \code{\verb~|code~}, \code{\verb~|code,casetrees~}, \code{\verb~|expect,code,casetrees~}, \code{\verb~|warm,code,casetrees~}, \code{\verb~|warm,gated,expect~}, \code{\verb~|warm,gated,expect,probes~}; \strong{not clean for \code{\verb~|gated,code,casetrees~}}. A tick on a path that only runs when a judgment is suspended, in the interplay of gated tabling and the K1 blocks.}
}

