\subtree{
\title{8.7 Incidents}

\ul{
\li{13:44Z-14:09Z: my first full gate (24 GB heap) was one of the processes on the host when it ran out of memory; I killed it by pid at 14:09Z. Since then every M8 job holds a slot and stays at 6 GB.}
\li{15:55Z: a \code{\verb~|pgrep -f~} pattern of mine matched the shell that issued it; that command ended my own shell and the slow-test script (intended); the test JVM it had started was then stopped by pid. Nothing of another agent was touched.}
\li{The two slow tests (\code{\verb~|M8SlowTest#convAll~}, \code{\verb~|M7HookedTest#all230~}) were started in the sandbox's surefire JVM at 15:45Z and stopped after 9 minutes to give the slot and 5 GB back when the host was at 16 GB available: \strong{they have not been run to completion under surefire since the change.} What stands in for them: the same code path (\code{\verb~|M8Lanes~} passes, heap failures as flagged declines) ran all 230 tests with five and six lanes in a 6 GiB JVM twice (the two gates above) without a crash, and the fast test \code{\verb~|aCheckThatTheJavaHeapEndsIsFlaggedAndTheLaneGoesOnWithANewMachine~}.}
}
}
}

